{%- comment -%}
  Cart overlap guard — store-wide.

  WHY THIS IS NOT PART OF THE BUNDLE LADDER. The ladder can only police the adds it
  handles itself. A shopper who takes the Complete Library from its own page and then
  walks to the Intrusive Thoughts Bundle and uses the main Add to cart never touches the
  ladder, and ends up holding both — which is the same broken promise the ladder was
  fixed to stop making, arrived at from the other direction. Upsell apps, quick-add,
  product cards and a cart restored from a previous session are all the same hole.

  So the rule lives with the cart instead of with any one button. It is rendered from
  layout/theme.liquid on every template, it re-checks after every cart change from any
  source, and it also checks on page load, which is what catches a cart that became
  redundant in another tab or on a previous visit.

  WHERE THE TRUTH LIVES. On the product, not in this file and not in a template: the
  `custom.bundle_includes` metafield on a bundle lists the products that bundle contains.
  One place to edit, and every surface — this guard, the ladder, anything added later —
  reads the same answer. A bundle with an empty metafield is inert: nothing about the
  cart changes until a merchant states what a bundle actually contains.

  THE VERDICT IS COMPUTED IN LIQUID, not in the browser. The script below never sees the
  metafields; it asks this section what to remove and does as it is told. That keeps the
  rule readable in one place and means the browser cannot be talked into deleting a line
  by anything other than the shop's own data.

  MUTUAL CONTAINMENT IS REFUSED. If two products each claim to include the other, that is
  a data-entry mistake, and honouring it would remove both and hand the shopper an empty
  cart. Neither is touched, so the mistake shows up as "nothing happened" rather than as
  a vanished order.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign rows = ''

  for item in cart.items
    assign covered_by = ''

    for other in cart.items
      unless other.key == item.key
        assign other_includes_item = false
        for included in other.product.metafields.custom.bundle_includes.value
          if included.id == item.product.id
            assign other_includes_item = true
            break
          endif
        endfor

        assign item_includes_other = false
        for included in item.product.metafields.custom.bundle_includes.value
          if included.id == other.product.id
            assign item_includes_other = true
            break
          endif
        endfor

        if other_includes_item
          unless item_includes_other
            assign covered_by = other.product.title
            break
          endunless
        endif
      endunless
    endfor

    if covered_by != blank
      capture row
        echo '{"key":'
        echo item.key | json
        echo ',"variant_id":'
        echo item.variant_id
        echo ',"quantity":'
        echo item.quantity
        echo ',"title":'
        echo item.product.title | json
        echo ',"covered_by":'
        echo covered_by | json
        echo '}'
      endcapture

      if rows != blank
        assign rows = rows | append: ','
      endif
      assign rows = rows | append: row
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  `lines` lets the script refuse a verdict that would empty the cart outright — a shape
  the rules above should never produce, and not a thing to find out about in production.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" data-blo-verdict>{"lines":{{ cart.items.size }},"remove":[{{ rows }}]}</script>

{%- if section.settings.enabled -%}
  <script
    type="module"
    src="{{ 'bundle-overlap.js' | asset_url }}"
    fetchpriority="low"
  ></script>

  <bundle-overlap
    data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
    data-cart-url="{{ routes.cart_url }}"
    data-add-url="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"
    data-update-url="{{ routes.cart_update_url }}"
    data-mode="{{ section.settings.mode }}"
    data-removed-message="{{ section.settings.removed_message | escape }}"
    data-ask-message="{{ section.settings.ask_message | escape }}"
    data-undo-label="{{ section.settings.undo_label | escape }}"
    data-remove-label="{{ section.settings.remove_label | escape }}"
    {% if request.design_mode %}data-design-mode{% endif %}
  >
    <div class="blo" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden data-blo-toast>
      <p class="blo__text" data-blo-text></p>
      <div class="blo__actions">
        <button type="button" class="blo__action" data-blo-action hidden></button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="blo__dismiss"
          data-blo-dismiss
          aria-label="{{ 'actions.close' | t | default: 'Close' }}"
        >
          &times;
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </bundle-overlap>

  {%- style -%}
    bundle-overlap { display: contents; }

    /*
      Fixed, and rendered outside .page-wrapper by theme.liquid for the reason its own
      comment gives: a transform or filter on an ancestor would trap it.
    */
    .blo {
      position: fixed;
      z-index: 100;
      inset-inline: 12px;
      bottom: calc(12px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
      margin-inline: auto;
      max-width: 30rem;
      display: flex;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 12px;
      padding: 12px 12px 12px 14px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--color-background, #0B0F0D);
      color: var(--color-foreground, #fff);
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 22%, transparent);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgb(0 0 0 / 28%);
      font-size: .82rem;
      line-height: 1.45;
    }
    .blo[hidden] { display: none; }

    .blo__text { margin: 0; flex: 1 1 auto; }
    .blo__actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; flex: 0 0 auto; }

    .blo__action {
      background: none; border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 4px 2px;
      font: inherit; font-weight: 700;
      color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px;
      cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .blo__action[hidden] { display: none; }

    .blo__dismiss {
      background: none; border: 0; margin: 0; padding: 0;
      width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 999px;
      font: inherit; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1;
      color: inherit; opacity: .6; cursor: pointer;
    }
    .blo__dismiss:hover { opacity: 1; }

    .blo__action:focus-visible,
    .blo__dismiss:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }

    @media (min-width: 750px) {
      .blo { inset-inline: auto 20px; bottom: 20px; margin-inline: 0; }
    }
  {%- endstyle -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart overlap guard",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Keeps the cart from holding a bundle and something that bundle already contains. List a bundle's contents in its \"Bundle includes\" metafield — with no metafield set, this does nothing."
    },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enabled", "label": "Enabled", "default": true },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "mode",
      "label": "When the cart holds an overlap",
      "options": [
        { "value": "remove", "label": "Remove it, with an Undo" },
        { "value": "ask", "label": "Ask before removing" }
      ],
      "default": "remove",
      "info": "Choose \"Ask\" where a bundle only partly covers the other product, so the shopper decides whether to give it up."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "removed_message",
      "label": "Message after removing",
      "default": "[items] came out of your cart — [bundle] already includes it."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "ask_message",
      "label": "Message when asking",
      "default": "[bundle] already includes [items]. Take it out of your cart?"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "undo_label", "label": "Undo button label", "default": "Undo" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "remove_label", "label": "Remove button label", "default": "Remove it" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Cart overlap guard" }]
}
{% endschema %}
